  data:  # ccf6
    kind: work_item  # ccf6
    title: "meta.evidence_lang null on 100% of 110533 edges incl spec-required cross-language"  # ccf6
    status: todo_hard  # ccf6
    priority: 1  # ccf6
    parent: INV-lifik-kasis-vadom-milom-pibat-surag-mivun-falob  # ccf6
    tags:  # ccf6
    - dogfood_tranch_03  # ccf6
    - dogfood  # ccf6
    isbefore: []  # ccf6
    duplicate_of: []  # ccf6
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ccf6
    pr_ref:  # ccf6
    description: "**Mechanic**: The producer pipeline never stamps `meta.evidence_lang` for the mainstream Python/JavaScript/HTML analyzers (only 21 long-tail language analyzers stamp it, and none of them produced edges on the self-corpus). The substrate-side count is 0 of 110,533. Within that 0%, the 63 cross-language edges that the spec explicitly marks as \"Required\" all have null `evidence_lang`. The spec's \"Default to src.language if omitted\" clause exists but the matrix lookup is also unimplemented, so even the documented fallback produces no signal. The producer-coherence linter accepts `None` as a legitimate value for an Optional[str] field, so both the consumer-side and producer-side gates pass the partial-adoption state as conformant.\n\n**Expectation**: Every edge carries `meta.evidence_lang`, with the spec-required cross-language sub-population unambiguously stamped; the producer-coherence linter rules that \"every Python edge MUST carry evidence_lang='python'\" (or equivalent), so partial-adoption states are caught.\n\n**Scope**: 110,533 of 110,533 edges (100%); the 63-edge cross-language sub-population is the most acute, since the spec calls the field \"Required\" specifically there.\n\n**Exposure**: Any consumer filtering cross-language edges, using the documented confidence matrix lookup, or trusting the `confidence_model: \"hypergumbo-evidence-v1\"` field's promise of a versioned deterministic algorithm.\n\n**Consequence**: The documented cross-language filter returns zero rows on every substrate; the confidence matrix is unmatchable; the `confidence_model` versioning promise is hollow on the most common producer pathway.\n\n**Source**: F49.A1 (INDEPENDENT, HIGH; F50.A2 absorbed as EXTENSION naming producer-side root cause; F54.A1 absorbed as EXTENSION re: cross-language sub-population).\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # ccf6
    fields: {}  # ccf6
- op: discuss  # 7205
  at: '2026-06-07T06:42:02Z'  # 7205
  by: agent  # 7205
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7205
  clock: 2  # 7205
  nonce: '7205'  # 7205
  message: "Dogfood fold (member F160.A2-a, split from F160.A2) — the edge evidence TRIPLE (evidence_lang, evidence_spans[], meta.evidence[]) is 0% populated on all 110533 edges, reproduces on the frozen substrate. The serializer drops these keys when None, and no producer sets them, so the keys are absent on every edge; only evidence_type (singular) and a coarse top-level line integer survive. Per-field counts: evidence_lang 0/110533, evidence_spans 0/110533, meta.evidence[] 0/110533; evidence_type present 110533/110533. Consequence: any consumer wanting precise localization of edge evidence (file+line+column of the call/import site), or wanting to know which language's analyzer produced a cross-language edge, gets only a single coarse line and cannot determine evidence language — weakening any audit of how the edge was inferred. The carding unit covers all three sub-fields, which the tracker already tracks as three distinct rows; this finding is folded onto each (WI-kuluh evidence_lang, WI-vozar evidence_spans, WI-gijus meta.evidence[]). The spec/done-marker side (§1530 🟩-done + §799 \"always reflect\" false) is filed separately as a net-new row (F160.A2-b)."  # 7205
- op: discuss  # af4a
  at: '2026-06-07T10:02:48Z'  # af4a
  by: agent  # af4a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # af4a
  clock: 3  # af4a
  nonce: af4a  # af4a
  message: "Dogfood re-confirmation. edge.meta.evidence_lang populated on 0/110533 edges. The spec-required cross-language sub-case is also 0: cross_language=True edges 29 (0 with evidence_lang), url_path(HTTP) edges 12 (0), channel(IPC) edges 145 (0). ir.py:731-734 to_dict serializes evidence_lang only when not None; no pass populates the in-memory field. The field is declared in schema.json:978-983 and marked done at spec line 1530 ('Required field presence (execution_id, run_signature, evidence_lang, evidence_spans)'), so the done-status over-claims a 0%-coverage field. A confidence-scoring consumer reading 'evidence_lang or src.language' (spec line 1176) always falls through to the src.language fallback."  # af4a
